  "term": "cumulative probability distribution",
  "definition": "A cumulative probability distribution is a curve that shows how probabilities add up across values, such as gray-scale pixel intensities in an image. In this context, it describes the accumulated distribution of plaque pixel gray levels and can reflect more of the overall pattern than a single summary value like the median.",
